<title>UK: LucasVarity firms amid talk of unit sale.</title>
<headline>LucasVarity firms amid talk of unit sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in newly merged LucasVarity Plc rose on Friday amid talk that the company may sell its aerospace arm to U.S. group United Technologies Corp of the U.S., traders said.</p>
<p>By 1034 GMT, the shares were up 8p at 248p on volume of 2.7 million shares.  </p>
<p>Rumours were that the unit was likely to command a price of around 600 million stg, said dealers.</p>
<p>No-one at Lucas was immediately available to comment on the speculation.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
</text>
